# Extract onboarding — no duplicate resident names on the same place

Document extract / fast-track import must not create two `users` rows for the same person on the same unit + building (e.g. two “Leslie Ann Douglas” on 109C).

When Residents shows duplicate names for the same lease place, delete the extra row (keep the richer / older profile) and harden import dedupe. Treat regressions as autofix.

## Rule

| Scenario | Required behavior |
|---|---|
| Same full name + unit + building in extract payload | One import row (`dedupeOnboardingImportResidents`) |
| Same person on AI review and final review | Merge into one `users` row (`onboardingResidentIdentityMatch`) |
| Residents list finds duplicate name+unit+building | Delete extras; do not leave both selectable for Start onboarding |

## Why it breaks activation

Household checkboxes select every member. A duplicate Leslie plus a roommate can send activation for the wrong ids, strip phones on collision, and surface `results` skipped/failed on Start onboarding.

## Autofix (Bugbot)

When a PR or bug report shows duplicate extracted residents on the same place:

1. Strengthen identity match / dedupe in `importResidents.ts` so same name+unit+building collapses before insert.
2. Prefer merging into an existing row over inserting a second id.
3. If duplicates already exist in DB, remove extras via `deleteResidentsForLandlord` (keep one canonical id with phone/activation when present).
4. Do not “fix” Start onboarding by only hiding duplicates in the UI while leaving two `users` rows.

## Where it lives

- Dedupe: `dedupeOnboardingImportResidents` / `onboardingResidentIdentityMatch` in `src/lib/onboarding/persist/importResidents.ts`
- Delete: `src/lib/residentDeletion.ts`
- List: `AdminResidentsDashboard` household grouping

## Do not

- Insert a second row because AI review and final review both listed the tenant
- Leave phone on only one duplicate while the Contact column implies both have it
- Skip autofix because “the landlord can delete manually”
